WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
- So the January 6 Committee

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.800
may have uncovered some
pretty serious crimes.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.040
After nearly a year of
investigating the January 6th attack

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.680
on the US Capitol, the House
Select Committee has started

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.660
to present their findings
to the American people

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.520
in a series of televised hearings.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.353
Since it's formation,

00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:17.310
the committee has conducted
over a thousand interviews

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.800
and reviewed more than 140,000 documents.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.080
The committee has also issued
more than a hundred subpoenas

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.900
for testimony and documents
as part of its inquiry,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.220
from a variety of individuals,

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.140
including Republican members of Congress,

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.200
former Trump White House
officials, outside Trump allies,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.350
like Roger Stone and Alex Jones
and white nationals figures

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.450
who've promoted false election claims.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.460
The committee has presented a
trove of evidence suggesting

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.293
that the Trump White House

00:00:39.293 --> 00:00:42.270
not only deliberately
undermined American democracy,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.520
but might have committed
crimes in the process.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.680
And the committee has even
told the federal court

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.150
that it believes the
former president himself

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.230
could be criminally prosecuted

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.760
for his conduct leading up to,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.330
and his actions on January 6, 2021.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.770
But what are the potential crimes

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:56.820
that former President Trump

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.630
and his cadre might have
committed related to January 6?

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.040
Well, there are a lot of them,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.290
and we're going to go
into detail for each one.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.820
Now, this is not an exhaustive survey

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.560
since the one, six committee
isn't finished yet,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.360
it's also fairly one-sided

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.130
because it is not a criminal prosecution

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.210
and it's not adversarial,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.130
so it's one side's presentation.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.580
Though many of the witnesses
are former Trump confidants,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.230
so take that for what you will.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.720
But in 2020, then President
Donald Trump was defeated

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.450
for reelection by former
Vice-President, Joe Biden

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.865
by a margin of 7 million
popular votes and account of 306

00:01:27.865 --> 00:01:30.480
to 232 votes in the electoral college.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.650
Since his lost, President Trump

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.570
has falsely insisted the
election was stolen from him

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.720
while repeating ridiculous
debugs conspiracy theories.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.580
Now these false accusations were endorsed

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.140
by many Republican members of Congress

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.160
and supporters in the media.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.840
Now between election day
and inauguration day,

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.190
President Trump and his allies sought

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.280
to overturn the results
by filing over 62 lawsuits

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.480
where they lost every single one,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.460
but a tiny part of one case
involving proximity to ballots

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.580
and made repeated allegations
of election fraud in the news,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.650
in social media, organized protests,

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.090
and tried to convince legislators

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.880
to take part in pressured
Georgia's secretary of state

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.890
to find enough votes to carry

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.060
that particular state.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.340
In addition, 84 Republicans
signed legal documents,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.800
falsely claiming to be
the duly chosen electors

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.050
for Donald Trump in the electoral college,

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.840
despite Trump having lost
in those particular states.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.120
These include dozens of local
Republican party leaders,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.950
seven candidates for public office,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.210
eight current office holders,

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:24.090
and at least five previous state
and federal office holders.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.390
This fake elector scheme was
led in part by Rudy Giuliani

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.130
and Trump lawyer, John Eastman,

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.400
the latter of whom penned
to now public memos

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.260
to pressure Vice-President Mike Pence

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.700
to overthrow the election results.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.383
And on January 6, 2021,

00:02:38.971 --> 00:02:39.900
a mob of Trump supporters
stormed to the US Capitol

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.240
to disrupt a joint session of Congress

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.830
that had convened to certify the results

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.300
of the 2020 election.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.230
Prior to that attack,

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.570
President Trump encouraged the
large crowd of his supporters

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.640
near the White House to
March on the US Capitol

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.150
and fight like hell to resist
Congress's certification

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.390
of the Biden victory, which
many in the crowd did.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.340
- [Crowd] USA, USA.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.320
- And approximately 140 Capitol

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.480
and metropolitan police officers
were criminally assaulted

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.320
in the attack.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.080
One died of a series of strokes
after being hospitalized

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.520
for his injury sustained in the attack,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.530
and two others committed suicide.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.690
One of the writers was shot
and killed by the police,

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:13.980
another died of a heart attack,

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.830
and a third was crushed to
death by the stampeding mob.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.110
Writers caused about
1.5 million in damages

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.370
to the Capitol building

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.050
and in response to the
House of Representatives

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.460
with 10 Republican votes,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.220
impeach Trump for
incitement of insurrection.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.860
Mr. Trump was acquitted
after only 57 senators,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.960
10 short of the required
two-thirds majority

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.400
voted to find him guilty.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.960
And even after the carnage on January 6,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.220
Trump continues to falsely claim

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.780
that the election was stolen from him.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.920
- It's all over the place,
it's massive election Fraud.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.890
- And in may of 2021 Senate
Republicans blocked the passage

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.210
of a house pass bill

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.890
that would've created
a national commission

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.020
to investigate the January 6th attack.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.270
In response, the house voted
to create a select committee

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.760
to investigate the January
6th attack on the US Capitol,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.500
speaker Pelosi rejected the appointments

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.290
of Republican representative,
Jim Jordan and Jim Banks

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.300
citing their objections
to the election results

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.100
on January 6, and raising concerns

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.440
that they would impact the
integrity of the investigation.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.870
In response house minority
leader, Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.820
pulled all remaining
Republicans on the committee,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.590
though Pelosi still named two impeachment,

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.170
supporting Republicans, Liz
Cheney and Adam Kinzinger

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.510
to serve on the select committee.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.640
Now much of the past year
has involved the prosecution

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.850
of over 800 January 6th
writers with charges ranging

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.890
from obstruction of an
official proceeding assault

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.150
to seditious conspiracy.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.040
But the January 6th hearings
are looking up the ladder

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.810
to see what crimes and to what extent

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.220
the Trump White House its allies,

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.370
and even Trump himself were
responsible for on that day.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.370
So let's look at some of the
potential criminal violations

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.320
of Trump and his circle.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.090
Now we first begin with
criminal conspiracy

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.530
to defraud the United States.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.537
Under 18 U.S.C. 371, it
is a criminal offense,

00:04:43.537 --> 00:04:45.330
"If two or more persons conspire,

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.640
either to commit any offense
against the United States

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.550
or to defraud the United
States or any agents thereof

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.980
in any manner or for any purpose."

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.170
The supreme court has held the
statute criminalizes the use

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.427
of deceptive practices in connection with,

00:04:57.427 --> 00:05:00.120
"Any conspiracy, for the purpose
of impairing, obstructing,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.680
or defeating the lawful function

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.840
of any department of government."

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.900
And conspiring to obstruct
a joint session of Congress

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.610
from certifying the election,

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.970
certainly qualifies as seeking
to obstruct a lawful function

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:12.930
of the government.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.270
Now to convict someone of
defrauding the United States,

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.820
the government must
establish three elements.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.680
One, at least two people
entered into an agreement

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.300
with the specific intent

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.030
to obstruct a lawful
function of government.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.610
Two, the individuals used
deceitful or dishonest means

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.110
to accomplish this goal.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.780
And three, at least one of
the conspirators engaged

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.020
in at least one overt act in
furtherance of the agreement.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.990
And to establish the requisite
intent for this crime,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.430
it's sufficient for the
prosecution to prove

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.380
that the defendant knew that
the statements were false

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.170
or fraudulent when made and
that such statements disrupted

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.910
the functions of the government.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.470
Accordingly, the January 6th Committee

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.600
has laid out a seven
point plan for how Trump

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.920
and his allies orchestrated

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.750
to defraud the United States government.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.550
One, they engaged in a considered effort

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.800
to spread false information
to the American public

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.360
that the 2020 election was stolen.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.760
Two, they orchestrated a
corrupt scheme between Trump,

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.170
his chief of staff, Mark Meadows

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.820
and representative Scott Perry

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.530
to replace the acting attorney general

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.110
who rejected Trump's fraud claims

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.270
with Trump DOJ ally, Jeffrey Clark

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.880
to use the justice department
to overturn the election.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.340
Three, they implemented a
plan by attorney John Eastman

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.560
into now public legal memos

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.320
to pressure Vice-President
Pence to refuse to count

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.930
or delay the certification
of the electoral count

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:25.350
despite Eastman's knowledge
that this violated federal law.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.240
For they pressured
state election officials

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.700
and state legislators to
change election results,

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.350
like Trump's infamous January 2nd,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.140
call to Georgia's secretary of
state, Bradford Raffensperger

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.230
to quote, "Find enough votes
to flip the state's results."

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.700
Five, they instructed Republicans,

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.260
including chief of staff, Mark Meadows,

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.660
acting at Trump's behest
in multiple states

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.510
to embrace Rudy Giuliani
and John Eastman's plan

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.400
to create a false electoral slate

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.000
in seven battleground states
and transmit those fake slates

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.190
to Congress and the national archives.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.830
Six, they summoned assembled
and incited a violent mob

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.650
in Washington and directed them
to March on the US Capitol.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.240
And seven, during the attack,

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.070
Trump ignored plead for assistance failed

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.870
to take immediate steps
to stop the violence

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.360
and even appeared to tacitly,
endorse the violence,

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.091
including threats to hang Mike Pence.

00:07:09.091 --> 00:07:10.397
- [Woman] Pence is a traitor.

00:07:11.557 --> 00:07:13.710
- [Woman] Traitor Pence, traitor Pence.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.270
- Now, it appears that
the phony elector scheme

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.500
has caught the DOJs attention,

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.630
having issued subpoenas
to several individuals

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.070
who signed false certificates,

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.750
including the chairs of the Georgia

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.220
and Arizona Republican Party.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:26.160
And in a March, 2022 crime
fraud exception ruling,

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.147
California, federal judge
David O. Carter found,

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:31.860
"It is more likely than not
that Trump and Eastman conspired

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:32.880
to defraud the United States

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.100
by corruptly attempting
to obstruct the counting

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.690
of electoral votes on January 6th."

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.670
But it remains to be seen whether the DOJ

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:41.850
will bring formal charges
against former President Trump

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.970
and his allies related to section 371,

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.980
but that takes us to obstructing
an official proceeding

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.650
of Congress under 18 U.S.C, 1512.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.030
Now that criminalizes the obstruction

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.250
or attempted obstruction
of an official proceeding

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.770
with a maximum prison
sentence of 20 years.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:57.663
To obtain a conviction,
prosecutors must establish

00:07:57.663 --> 00:08:00.930
that the person obstructed
influence or impeded or attempted

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.960
to obstruct influence or
impede an official proceeding

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.660
of the United States and did so corruptly.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.920
Courts have uniformly held

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.450
that the January 6th joint session

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.800
is an official proceeding,

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.560
and hundreds of Capitol
writers have been charged

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:14.430
with this crime.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.140
And for many, this is the only felony

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.640
that they were charged with.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.107
This includes Jacob Chansley,

00:08:19.107 --> 00:08:21.480
the so-called QAnon
Shaman who pleaded guilty

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.580
to a single charge of corruptly impeding

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.380
an official proceeding and was sentenced

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.510
to 41 months in prison.

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:29.070
Now, the legal theory for prosecution

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.110
is that former president Trump in concert

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.570
with allies like Eastman,
Clark Meadows and others

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.310
intentionally or corruptly interfered

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:38.070
with Congress's certification
of electoral votes,

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.750
despite aggressive pushback

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.660
that not only were these plans illegal,

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.340
but that there was no reasonable basis

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.080
to doubt that Biden won.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.590
Now, multiple members of Trump's
circle testified under oath

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.750
to the select committee
that they all told Trump

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.610
his claims of election
fraud were baseless,

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.560
including Attorney General Bill Barr,

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.150
Campaign Aide Jason Miller,

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:59.220
Mike Pence's former Chief
of Staff Marc Short,

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.380
and even his own daughter Ivanka.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:03.900
And though Trump circle told
him his claims were baseless,

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.640
his supporters took those claims as gospel

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.610
to justify storming Capitol
to deny certification.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.460
- I'm here to protest this corruption.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.070
We wanna stop the deal,
we want a free election,

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.840
we want Donald Trump in office.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:18.480
- The committee's first
hearing on January 9th

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.390
showed previous unseen footage
of writers, many whom said

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.490
they were following
President Trump's commands

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:24.330
to storm the Capitol

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.980
to block the certification of election,

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.200
they were told was stolen.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.730
- And people are really pissed off

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.950
because we know how
much cheating took place

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.300
and if'd won fair and square,

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.380
I think we would be fine,

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.230
but we can't let them
overthrow our country.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:39.000
- And the mob believing
these election lies

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.000
did successfully delay the
account for at least seven hours

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.630
by violently forcing both
chambers into recess and hiding.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.010
Trump's reported obstruction scheme

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.020
also involves strong arming the DOJ

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.370
to overturn the election.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.380
And contemporaneous notes of acting

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.450
Deputy Attorney General,
Richard Donoghue showed

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.317
that Trump asked him directly to,

00:09:56.317 --> 00:09:58.320
"Say that the election was corrupt

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.490
and leave the rest to him, and
the Republican Congressman.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.540
Suggesting that Trump didn't

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.950
want a good faith investigation,

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.870
just a DOJ declaring as cover

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.140
for throwing out Biden's
dually elected electoral votes.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:13.080
And accordingly the select
committee has presented evidence

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.670
that Trump and others corruptly obstructed

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.370
an official proceeding by
advancing legal strategies.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.440
They knew were unlawful
based on allegations

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.580
of election fraud,

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.990
and they had no reasonable basis

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.190
to believe that they were true.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.350
But prosecution under
section 15, 12, depends

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.900
on how federal courts
interpret that statute.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.720
In March of 2022 DC Judge Carl Nichols,

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.000
a Trump appointee who
has issued more lenient

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.190
January six sentences
compared to his colleagues

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.220
broke with at least seven
other DC federal judges

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.130
by ruling that the DOJ
cannot charge individuals

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:42.540
with obstructing Congress,

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.040
unless the defendant's actually tampered

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.860
with official documents
or records on January 6.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.900
So this could potentially
impact hundreds of cases,

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.660
including the potential prosecution
of Trump and his circle.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.270
And that takes us to
garden variety wire fraud.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.103
Between election day

00:10:55.103 --> 00:10:58.140
and leaving office on January 20th, 2021.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.660
Then President Trump raised
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.990
for what he told supporters
was to contest the results.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:07.080
There's just one, 250 million problem.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.690
Trump raised millions for
an election defense fund

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.150
that may not actually exist.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.890
Sometimes suggested
this could be wire fraud

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:17.040
under 18 U.S.C. 1343 wire fraud occurs

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.800
when someone uses interstate
communications devices

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.633
like a cell phone,

00:11:20.633 --> 00:11:24.360
the computer or other electronic
device to advances scheme

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:26.040
to defraud another.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.270
To prove wire fraud the government

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.500
has to establish four elements.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.120
One, that the defendant voluntarily

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.580
and intentionally devised
or participated in a scheme

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.680
to defraud another out of money.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.110
That the defendant did so
with the intent to defraud

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.490
that it was reasonably foreseeable

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.740
that interstate wire
communications would be used,

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.560
and that interstate wire
communications were in fact used.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.330
To convict Trump of wire fraud prosecutors

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.450
would have to show that he
solicited funds for one purpose

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.580
and knowingly used them for another.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.740
The January 13th hearing led

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:55.560
by Congresswoman Zoe Lofgren of California

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.350
showed that the campaign spent
very little of this money

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.580
on election contests.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.940
And instead funneled the money
to among other destinations

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.110
Trump business properties

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.720
and his own Save America
political action committee.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.600
This fundraising scheme might
potentially be fraudulent,

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.310
not just because it induced donations

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.690
with claims of voter fraud,

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.310
which Trump had been repeatedly informed

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.540
by the justice department and others

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.980
that they were baseless,

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.810
but also because the money did not go

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.030
to where people thought
it was going to go.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:23.280
This would be a particularly
hard claim to prove,

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.320
but there is precedent
for prosecuting candidates

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.910
who raised money for fake organizations

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.710
and then spend the funds on themselves.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:31.980
In 2019, Harold Russell
Taub, Rhode Island Republican

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.090
who ran unsuccessfully

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:36.990
against democratic Congressman
David Cicilline in 2016,

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.990
pleaded guilty to wire fraud
and campaign finance violations

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.960
in connection with a 1.6 million raise

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.120
for a non-existent
political action committee.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.370
In the course of fundraising
Taub told his donors

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.900
that his PAC staff were volunteers

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.790
and that a hundred
percent of the donations

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.980
would be used to support
Republican candidates in Ohio

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.750
at the state and federal level.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.850
In reality, the two PACs were unregistered

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.190
and Taub spent $1 million of those funds

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.630
on personal expenses.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.820
Adding to the deception
Taub falsely told donors

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:06.600
that he was an ambassador and
also used without permission

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:09.030
a former secretary of the Navy
in his fundraising appeal,

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.160
despite being repeatedly told to stop.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.080
Taub was sentenced to three
years in federal prison

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.180
in order to repay 1.1 million

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.520
that he made through his fraudulent PACs.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.920
Now, ironically Trump's best
defense against wire fraud

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.170
would be to argue that
he sincerely did believe

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:24.690
that the funds would be used
to fight election contest.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:25.680
And for the mercurial

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.450
and potentially sincere Donald Trump,

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.250
that could be a challenge for prosecutors.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.930
But that takes us to criminal solicitation

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.650
to commit election fraud and
other Georgia state crimes.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.080
Now it seems like Trump
is particularly vulnerable

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.390
to a litany of state charges in Georgia

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.360
where Fulton County District
Attorney Fani Willis

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.910
has convened a special grand
jury to investigate Trump

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.580
and his allies efforts to
pressure election officials

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:49.440
and change the vote count in Georgia.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.590
By letter dated February
10th, 2021 DA Willis announced

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:55.410
that her office had, "Opened
an investigation into attempts

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.850
to influence the administration

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.830
of the 2020 general election."

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.090
And where Trump and his allies

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:02.340
probably find the most
potential criminal exposure

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.550
is Georgia Code Section 21-2-604,

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.520
the criminal solicitation
to commit election fraud,

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:10.890
which can be charged as either
a misdemeanor or felony.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:14.370
And to establish a violation
under Section 21-2-604,

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.290
the DA has to show that
the defendant has one,

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.450
solicited, requested,
commanded, importuned,

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.310
or otherwise attempted
to cause another person

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:21.780
to engage in election fraud.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.210
And two, the defendant actually intends

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.250
for the other person to
commit election fraud.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:28.050
And at the center of this potential crime

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.730
are the two recorded phone calls

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.590
involving the president applying pressure

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.690
to state election
officials to flip the state

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.760
from Biden to himself.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:39.210
First, on December 23rd, 2020,
Trump urged Francis Watson,

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:42.270
the chief election investigator
for Georgia's secretary

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.667
of state office, to
find fraud telling her,

00:14:45.667 --> 00:14:48.570
"When the right answer comes
out, you'll be praised."

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.780
And second in the famous
January 2nd, 2021 recorded

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.880
phone call to Georgia secretary of state,

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:56.100
Brad Raffensperger, where
the former president

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.607
famously demanded that he,

00:14:57.607 --> 00:15:01.140
"Find 11,780 votes,"

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.720
one more than Trump needed
to win in that state.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.307
- [Trump] I just wanna find 11,780 votes,

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.710
which is one more than we have.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:15.840
- When Ravensburger rejected
Trump's false claims

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.760
of voter fraud, like
the (indistinct) claim

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.010
that the Trump votes were thrown out,

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:23.130
while suitcases of votes were
carried in for Joe Biden,

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.410
Trump suggested Raffensperger
could face criminal charges,

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.150
telling him it would be illegal

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.990
and a big risk to
resolve against reporting

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.210
Trump's false claims.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:35.490
Trump also implicitly
threatened other state officials

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.440
with jail time, and
continues to hold a grudge

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.660
against every Georgia elected official

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.070
who refuses his demands.

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:42.270
- So what are we gonna do here, folks?

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:45.000
I only need 11,000 votes, fellas.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.700
I need 11,000 votes, give me a break.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:49.590
- And in addition to criminal solicitation

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:52.170
of election fraud, DA Willis has indicated

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:54.450
that her officers' investigation involves

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.700
other potential violations
of Georgia law by Trump

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.840
and his associates, including,

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:01.260
but not limited to, "The
making of false statements

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:03.360
to state and local governmental bodies,"

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.540
that's Georgia Code Section 16-10-20.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.460
Conspiring to commit election fraud,

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:12.870
that's Georgia Code Section 21-2-603.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:17.460
Racketeering, Georgia
Code Section 16-14-4.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:21.210
Violation of oath of
office, Section 16-10-1.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.210
And any involvement in
violence or threats related

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.620
to the election administration.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:30.517
That's Georgia Code
Section 21-2-566 and 597.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.990
Now, illustrating the expanded
scope of the investigation,

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:36.060
the grand jury has subpoenaed
several key members

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.790
of the Trump legal team
that advised his campaign

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.250
on how to overturn
Biden's wins in Georgia,

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.650
and other swing states,
including John Eastman,

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.930
Cleta Mitchell, Kenneth Chesebro,

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:47.820
Jenna Ellis, and Rudy Giuliani,

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.070
who twice presented
Georgia state legislators

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.590
with fake evidence and
wild conspiracy theories,

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:54.720
even after they were debunked.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.700
The grand jury has also
subpoenaed US Senator,

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.860
Lindsay Graham, who
twice asked Raffensperger

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:01.200
if there was any way to
throw out mail-in ballots,

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.610
which were favoring Joe Biden.

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:04.770
According to the subpoena,
Graham asked Raffensperger

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.840
and his staff, "about reexamining

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.850
certain absentee ballots cast in Georgia

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.680
in order to explore the possibility

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.080
of a more favorable outcome for Trump."

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:15.030
Describing the call to
CNN, Raffensperger said

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:17.340
the Senator was implying
that his office should try

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.990
to throw away ballots.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.490
- I got the sense it implied

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:23.130
that then you could throw those out.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:25.380
- But that takes us to another
potential federal charge,

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:28.080
which would be the incitement
to riot and insurrection.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.300
Trump was acquitted of
incitement to insurrection

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:31.440
in his second impeachment trial,

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.630
but since that was not a judicial trial,

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.190
there's no double jeopardy problem,

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:36.900
and he could potentially face charges

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.210
on various incitement statutes.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:42.810
Under the Anti-Riot Act
18 U.S.C. Section 2101,

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.900
anyone who uses interstate
travel to incite, organize,

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.420
participate in, or carry on a riot,

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.180
or commit any other act
of violence in furtherance

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:54.840
of a riot, or aid or abet
a person doing the above

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.400
is guilty of a federal crime punishable

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.960
by up to five years in prison.

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.530
And under Section 18 U.S.C. 2383,

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:04.830
anyone who incites, assists,
or engages in any rebellion

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.140
or insurrection against the
authority of the United States,

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.240
or gives aid or in comfort there too

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:11.160
is subject to up to 10
years in imprisonment

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:13.320
and disqualification from
holding public office.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.970
Now, conviction under
either of these statutes

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.260
would be incredibly difficult,

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.910
because political speech tends

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.790
to be at the very core
of the First Amendment,

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:22.740
and you generally have
a First Amendment right

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.780
to make these kinds of speeches.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.640
But in Brandenburg versus Ohio,

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.770
the Supreme Court
established a two-part test

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.170
for when the government may
criminalize speech advocating

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.030
for the use of force or crime.

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:35.820
One, the speech is directed to inciting

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:38.220
and producing imminent lawless action,

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:42.030
and the speech is likely to
incite or produce such action.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.100
And it would be incredibly fraught to try

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.260
to prove that Trump intended

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.890
to incite imminent lawless
action on January 6th.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.900
Though many writers did say on

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.670
and after January 6th that
they marched on the Capitol,

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:55.680
specifically because Trump told them to.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:58.830
- I'm here to support the president,

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.870
I think the election was a fraud.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.700
- And with respect to the second criteria,

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.990
the committee has presented evidence

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.450
that Trump not only incited
the mob to go to the Capitol,

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:09.360
but Trump endorsed the
violence of the people he saw

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.190
when they were there on his behalf.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.560
Cassidy Hutchinson, the
former aid to chief of staff.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.150
Mark Meadows provided bombshell testimony

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.240
that Trump was aware that
many people outside his rally

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.210
were armed with knives,
guns in the form of pistols,

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.690
and rifles, bear spray, body
armor, spears and flag poles.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:28.200
And he didn't care because
they were, "my people."

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.520
Hutchinson further testified

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.537
that she heard Trump say
something to the effect of,

00:19:31.537 --> 00:19:33.960
"I don't (beep) care
that they have weapons,

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.520
they're not here to hurt me.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.720
Take the (beep) mags,

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.910
the magnetometers and
metal detectors away.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.760
Let my people in, they can
March on the Capitol from here.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:44.430
Let the people in, take
the (beep) mags away."

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.590
And Hutchinson also testified
that when Trump was told

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.200
about the writers' hang Mike Pence chants,

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.127
Trump approvingly responded,

00:19:51.127 --> 00:19:54.270
"Maybe our supporters have the right idea,

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.740
Mike Pence deserves it."

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.780
Now, furthermore, the Joint Chiefs'

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.730
Chairman General Mark Milley testified

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.500
that Pence ordered National Guard troops

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.630
to defend the Capitol, while
Trump allowed the violence

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.040
to continue unabated.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.200
We also know that Trump waited 187 minutes

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.660
before putting out a
statement asking for calm.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:12.090
Now, it was always going to
be a long shot to charge Trump

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.610
with incitement, though the testimony

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.220
that has been elicited
so far probably comes

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.800
as close as you might be able to get.

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.980
And multiple sources say that
Trump had actual knowledge

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:25.320
that his speech was going
to incite his supporters,

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.420
particularly the armed
ones to go to the Capitol

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:30.870
before Trump allowed the
violence to rage for three hours.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.950
So who knows here?

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.380
But that takes us to
two potential new crimes

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.850
that were uncovered,

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.070
witness tampering and
obstruction of justice.

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.350
Many people say it's not
the crime, it's the coverup,

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:43.050
and that may be the case here as well.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.930
After Hutchinson's testimony,
Trump ex chief of staff,

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.730
Mick Mulvaney, suggested on Twitter

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.560
that his former boss could be vulnerable

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:51.840
to witness tampering and
obstruction of justice.

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.220
So what would that entail?

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:56.100
Well, 18 U.S.C. 15, 12, the same statute

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.410
that includes obstruction
of an official proceeding,

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.120
broadly criminalizes witness tampering

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:02.010
with up to 20 years imprisonment.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.570
This section makes it a crime for anyone

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.880
who knowingly uses intimidation, threats,

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.890
or otherwise attempts to
persuade another person

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.710
to change, delay, or prevent testimony,

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.860
or any person in an official proceeding.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:15.390
After Hutchinson's testimony,

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.970
the select committee produced
examples of witnesses

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:20.760
being asked by people
apparently close to Trump

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.980
to be loyal to him and his administration.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.890
Representative Liz Cheney
said an unnamed witness told

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:28.770
the committee, "What they
said to me is, as long

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.660
as I continue to be a team player,

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:32.340
they know I'm on the right team,

00:21:32.340 --> 00:21:33.570
I'm doing the right thing,

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:35.400
I'm protecting who I need to protect.

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:36.840
You know, I'll continue to stay

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:38.640
in good graces in Trump World.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.860
And they have reminded
me a couple of times

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.050
that Trump does read the transcripts."

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:44.730
And the second example Cheney cited

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:47.047
was a call a witness received saying,

00:21:47.047 --> 00:21:50.430
"A person, let me know you
have your deposition tomorrow.

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:52.800
He wants me to let you know,
he's thinking about you.

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:54.030
He knows you're loyal,

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:55.590
and you're going to do the right thing

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.600
when you go in for your deposition."

00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:59.010
The select committee has suggested

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:01.200
there are many more
examples of similar efforts

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:02.430
to influence witnesses.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:06.120
And with respect to obstruction
of justice, 18 U.S.C. 1505,

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:08.490
that criminalizes the act or the attempt

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:10.740
to corruptly influence, obstruct,

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:13.050
or impede a congressional investigation

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.070
through threats, force,

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:16.110
or threatening
communications, with a penalty

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:17.520
of up to five years imprisonment.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.490
Now, corruptly means acting
with an improper purpose,

00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.440
personally, or by influencing another,

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:24.720
including making a false
or misleading statement,

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.610
or withholding, concealing, altering,

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:28.980
or destroying a document
or other information.

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:32.340
And before her public
appearance, Hutchinson told

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:34.200
the committee that
several Republican members

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.660
of the far-right House
Freedom Caucus asked

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:39.480
for preemptive blanket
pardons for themselves

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:41.280
and others in connection
with their efforts

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:42.390
to overturn the election,

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.880
including Representatives
Mo Brooks, Matt Gaetz,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.420
Andy Biggs, and Louie
Gohmert and Scott Perry.

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:50.460
Hutchinson also said Jim Jordan asked

00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:52.440
for an update on presidential pardons

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:54.150
without asking for one directly,

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:55.470
and she heard from another staffer

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:58.650
that Marjorie Taylor Green
had asked for a pardon.

00:22:58.650 --> 00:23:01.620
These preemptive pardon
requests could be an effort

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:05.070
to induce those involved, or are witnesses

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:06.930
to criminal conduct to remain silent,

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:11.100
which even with a president's
nearly unlimited pardon power

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:13.020
might constitute criminal violations.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:15.300
Hutchinson also told the
committee that she witnessed

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:18.030
Meadows burn documents after
a meeting in his office

00:23:18.030 --> 00:23:19.620
with Representative Scott Perry,

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:20.880
and the destruction of documents,

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:24.030
coupled with Perry's request
for a pardon might suggest

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:26.190
the pair understood that they
were doing something illegal,

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:28.080
which could be evidence
of witness tampering,

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.150
and/or obstruction of justice.

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:32.580
And that takes us to seditious conspiracy.

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.530
At the first hearing of
the select committee,

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:36.480
Representative Cheney
declared that the committee

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.210
will detail plots to
commit seditious conspiracy

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.190
on January 6th.

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:43.920
Now, this is among the most
serious of crimes alleged

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:47.280
with sedation, essentially
being just a step below treason.

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:49.650
To convict individuals
of seditious conspiracy

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:53.070
under 18 U.S.C. 2384,
prosecutors would have

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.900
to establish that at
least two people conspired

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.850
to use force to overthrow the government,

00:23:56.850 --> 00:24:01.020
oppose its authority, or
subvert the execution of US law.

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:02.940
These charges are understandably rare,

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:04.860
but they were brought against some members

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:06.750
of the far-right Oath
Keepers and Proud Boys,

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:09.150
including their former
Chairman Enrique Tarrio,

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:13.260
for conspiring to use armed
force to violently oppose

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.390
the peaceful transfer
of presidential power.

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:18.390
So what might seditious
conspiracy charges against Trump

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:19.770
or his circle look like?

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:21.990
Well, after the first
meeting, committee chair,

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:24.930
Representative Benny Thompson
told CNN that witnesses

00:24:24.930 --> 00:24:27.270
had described conversations
between far-right extremists

00:24:27.270 --> 00:24:28.410
and Trump's circle...

00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:29.490
And direct communications

00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:32.490
with Oath Keepers and Proud
Boys could be concrete evidence

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:34.920
of White House involvement
in the same crimes.

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:37.680
It's hard to say we haven't
seen that evidence yet.

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:39.960
So just conspiracy
might also involve Trump

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:41.700
and his allies allowing the violence

00:24:41.700 --> 00:24:43.577
to continue to pressure Pence.

00:24:43.577 --> 00:24:46.410
(indistinct) to the president's demands

00:24:46.410 --> 00:24:48.540
to not certify the results.

00:24:48.540 --> 00:24:50.310
In fact, days after the attack,

00:24:50.310 --> 00:24:53.100
we learned that Trump and
Rudy Giuliani had urged

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:56.160
at least one GOP Senator
to stall the proceedings

00:24:56.160 --> 00:24:57.840
while the violence unfolded.

00:24:57.840 --> 00:24:59.670
Though there are certainly
not a lot of examples

00:24:59.670 --> 00:25:02.160
of successful seditious
conspiracy prosecutions

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:03.720
in the last 100 years.

00:25:03.720 --> 00:25:06.660
Though in 1995, Sheikh Omar Abdel-Rahman,

00:25:06.660 --> 00:25:09.450
a prominent Muslim clerk and
nine others, were convicted

00:25:09.450 --> 00:25:11.370
of seditious conspiracy for planning

00:25:11.370 --> 00:25:13.320
to bomb the New York City landmarks

00:25:13.320 --> 00:25:15.840
after the 1993 World Trade Center bombing.

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:18.210
Conspiracy charges have been difficult

00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:20.130
to make stick, particularly
against far-right groups,

00:25:20.130 --> 00:25:23.610
given the Brandenburg
protection of illegal advocacy

00:25:23.610 --> 00:25:25.530
without imminent lawless action.

00:25:25.530 --> 00:25:28.830
But by May, 2022, three Oath
Keepers had pleaded guilty

00:25:28.830 --> 00:25:30.060
to those charges.

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:32.880
And if these defendants
cooperated in their plea deals,

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:35.310
it might shed light on whether members

00:25:35.310 --> 00:25:38.400
of the Trump White House
and his circle could face

00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:40.500
their own seditious conspiracy charges.

00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:41.880
